  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city's decision to invest in renewable energy has been met with both praise and criticism. While some argue that it will create jobs and reduce the city's carbon footprint, others claim that the costs are too high and the benefits are uncertain.\n\nA recent study by a leading environmental organization found that the city's current reliance on fossil fuels is not only harming the environment but also contributing to respiratory problems in its citizens. However, the same study also highlighted the potential for renewable energy to provide a significant source of income for the local community.\n\nDespite these findings, some critics argue that the investment in renewable energy is a 'waste of taxpayers' money.' They claim that the costs will be passed on to consumers through higher electricity bills and that the benefits will not be felt for many years to come.\n\nHowever, supporters of the decision point out that the long-term savings from reduced energy consumption and lower maintenance costs will far outweigh the initial investment. They also argue that the creation of new jobs and industries will bring a significant boost to the local economy.\n\nIn conclusion, while there are valid concerns about the cost-effectiveness of investing in renewable energy, the potential benefits for both the environment and the community make it a worthwhile decision.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The city's investment in renewable energy will have no impact on its citizens.\", \"The costs of investing in renewable energy are too high and the benefits are uncertain.\", \"The city's decision to invest in renewable energy has been met with both praise and criticism.\", \"The study highlighted the potential for renewable energy to provide a significant source of income for the local community.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the passage, what is one of the benefits of investing in renewable energy?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It will create jobs and reduce the city's carbon footprint.\", \"It will provide a significant source of income for the local community.\", \"It will increase the city's reliance on fossil fuels.\", \"It will have no impact on the environment.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the author imply about the critics' views on investing in renewable energy?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The author agrees with their concerns and thinks they are valid.\", \"The author disagrees with their concerns and thinks they are unfounded.\", \"The author is neutral and doesn't take a stance.\", \"The author implies that the critics' views are based on misinformation.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What does the passage suggest about the long-term effects of investing in renewable energy?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They will be negative and have a significant impact on the local economy.\", \"They will be neutral and have no impact on the environment.\", \"They will be positive and bring significant savings to consumers.\", \"They are unknown and cannot be predicted.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards investing in renewable energy?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The author is neutral and doesn't take a stance.\", \"The author thinks it is a waste of taxpayers' money.\", \"The author believes it is a worthwhile decision despite some concerns.\", \"The author thinks it will have no impact on the environment.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
